what's going on guys this is rob and we  are back again with another installment  of our beyond omega level series where  we break down the most powerful  characters in comics and this week we're  going to talk about a character that was  suggested by one of our viewers taiwan  1984 who suggested that we cover hunger  the devourer of realities now this is a  character that was created by jim  starlin and first appeared in thanos  number one in 2003 so this story  basically opens up with thanos just kind  of sitting alone honestly kind of moping  around and he's visited by adam warlock  who has tracked him to this location and  is concerned that he's going to destroy  the nearby planet of rigel 3 home to a  race known as the rajelians who are a  really cool race actually they created  the recorders but to warlock surprise  however thanos seems to have turned over  a new leaf and is actually there to make  amends and help the regellians with  whatever it is they need because he  terrorized them in the past so thanos  and warlock go to the regellian planet  and learn that there is something the  regellians need help with on another one  of the planets they've colonized rigel  18. now when they arrive they find that  the planet faces a major potential  catastrophe as galactus ship has been  parked nearby indicating that he isn't  planning on consuming the world because  if he were he would have just already  done so all the while we also see panels  depicting a pair of glowing eyes  commenting that everything is going  according to plan so after thanos tries  and fails to learn galactus plans by  meeting with him telepathically galactus  puts his plan into action he uses his  technology not to consume rigel 18 but  to cause its sun to explode now galactus  then ventures into the dying star where  a portal to another reality has  basically formed and so galactus reaches  in and pulls out a skeleton with a  purple gem on its chest then the  disembodied glowing eyes we saw earlier  break the fourth wall and begin speaking  directly to us as the reader so what  ends up happening is this thing  basically introduces itself as hunger  and discloses that it has recently  become aware of the existence of the  main marvel universe when it observed  the energy produced during the infinity  gauntlet saga now because the energy  burst was brief hunger was only alerted  to the existence of the universe but  could not pinpoint its location so it  waited until magus the evil aspect of  adam warlock united the infinity gems  when it learned the location of this  universe of course that happened during  the events of infinity war however  because the universe was spherical  hunger could not enter it on his own but  needed an unwitting accomplice with  sufficient power and an exploitable  weakness in order to help it so  basically hunger tricks galactus into  thinking the vibrational patterns of the  infinity gems were identical to those of  the living energy he needed to survive  and so galactus then constructs a device  which he thinks will siphon energy off  of the infinity gems which will allow  him to stop consuming populated worlds  because it's one of the things that he  hates he hates consuming worlds but the  true purpose of the device is to open a  portal to allow hunger into the marvel  universe because hunger is like galactus  in that it is a devourer but while  galactus devours planets hunger devours  reality so think of hunger as a less  interesting version of the black winter  from donny kate's thor run but hunger  doesn't divulge anything about its  origin it does however reveal its  motivation for coming to the main marvel  universe while also saying that his plan  to devour the universe simply cannot be  stopped and so when galactus finally  gathers the infinity gems and then opens  the portal he's shocked when it does not  unlock a limitless energy source but  instead grants hunger entry into the  universe now galactus summons all of his  power and blasts hunger but hunger  simply consumes it as nourishment he  quite literally eats the power cosmic  and so it's clear from this altercation  that even the combined forces of thanos  and galactus are vastly overpowered by  hunger and it's only because thanos has  devised a clever scheme to transport the  old rigel 3 to impact rigel 18 and place  the nuclear warhead at the detonation  point that they're able to gain a  victory over hunger however after the  explosion we see hunger has survived and  then flies off into space seemingly  setting up a return now the return  wouldn't come until 2018's thanos the  infinity siblings graphic novel which  explains that hunger spent eons floating  through space basically being a shell of  its former self then it encounters a  planet full of beings it could absorb  and steadily increased in power until it  was able to kill a version of thanos  that is vastly more powerful than the  last time they fought however thanos is  able to travel to a point in time  centuries before that happens and kill  hunger before he's able to regain his  power now it would be revealed in 2019's  the infinity ending that it was actually  adam warlock who used the soul gem to  give hunger a boost of power that he  needed to conquer the planet zeltya  which led him to being able to defeat  the nearly omnipotent version of thanos  that he defeated in the infinity  siblings and of course we haven't really  seen hunger make an appearance since  then and who knows when or if jim  starlin will ever go back and work with  marvel again as the infinity ending was  billed as the last chapter of the thanos  story that he'd been telling for decades  so we really have no idea if we'll ever  see hunger again in a marvel comic book  at this point it seems unlikely and in  all honesty it's not the biggest loss  but just to recap this guy's powers he  literally consumes entire realities i  mean he's like galactus but just one  step higher on the food chain and his  devouring of realities makes galactus  devouring of planets seem like child's  play hunger also has very powerful  telepathic abilities as evidenced by the  fact that he was able to take a being as  powerful as galactus and basically use  him as an unwitting pawn to do his  bidding without having a clue that he  was being manipulated and galactus is a  being that has cosmic awareness and so  the fact that hunger made him its puppet  from a completely different reality is  pretty freaking impressive now hunger  also states that he can effortlessly  travel between parallel dimensions and  only has difficulty with spherical  dimensions like the main marvel universe  and there appears to be no limit to  hunger's potential power level as he was  able to become so powerful by infecting  and absorbing other beings that he took  down a nearly omnipotent version of  thanos and that's basically all there is  to know about the character he hasn't  really appear very often and like i said  i doubt he'll show up anytime soon for a  character as powerful as he is he's  pretty cartoonish which might be why he  hasn't really caught on outside of jim  starlin's books but i do like to fulfill  fan requests from time to time so leave  them in the comments if you have any  thank you guys for watching and i will  catch you all later  peace
 

